course: dictionary
lesson: 7797
title: Quarantine: keeping apart to stop spreading
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Quarantine can be a time of keeping apart, or a verb meaning to keep someone apart. «Medieval towns kept travellers apart for forty days, which is where the word quarantine comes from.» The words kept apart and forty are your clues.
explain: Quarantine is a time when a person or animal who may have a catching disease is kept away from others, so the disease does not spread. When you meet it, ask: what would fit here? Try «kept away from others» in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: As a verb, to quarantine someone means to keep them apart for this reason. In computing, to quarantine a file means to lock it away because it may have a virus. The idea is the same each time: something is kept apart so it cannot harm others.
fact: Quarantine means keeping a person or animal apart from others, so that a catching disease does not spread.
fact: «Quarantine» can also be a verb: to quarantine someone means to keep them apart for this reason.
fact: In computing, to quarantine a file means to lock it away because it may have a virus.
fact: Common phrases are «in quarantine», «go into quarantine», «quarantine period» and «under quarantine».
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, strict quarantine stops pests and diseases arriving on food, plants and animals at the airport.
exercise: «Ships with sick sailors were kept in quarantine.» What does quarantine mean here? | Sailing very fast across the sea | Painted in bright colours | *Kept apart from others so the sickness does not spread | Given a big party on board
exercise: To quarantine a file means to do what? | Delete it for fun | Send it to a friend | *Lock it away because it may have a virus | Print it in colour
exercise: «Pets coming from abroad may need quarantine.» What does quarantine stop from arriving? | Birthday cards | Sunshine and rain | *Pests and diseases | Tourists on holiday
test: Which word means a time of keeping apart to stop a disease spreading? | Whisper | Holiday | *Quarantine | Mountain
test: What is the common phrase for being kept apart because of a disease? | at the top | in a rush | in the bath | *in quarantine
exam: «Quarantine comes from the Italian word for» what number? | Four hundred | *Forty | Ten | Twelve
